      "id": "c:4974409897",
      "kind": "interface",
      "harm": "implicit first-index usage is unobvious to reviewers and complicates multi_index reimplementation",
      "quote": "please specify an index for each operation, as opposed to just using `m_txs`. What happens behind the scenes in that case is that the first index is used, which is not _at all_ obvious to reviewers.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "author_replies": [
        "c:5027545920"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": true,
      "settled_by_id": "c:5027545920",
      "settled_by_quote": "I've changed all of the `modify` to `extract` then `insert`, with some changes to the functions that iterate over everything in the wallet."
    },
    {
      "id": "c:4974409897",
      "kind": "approach",
      "harm": "modify has complex re-insertion failure semantics and is incompatible with standard container APIs",
      "quote": "please use `extract`/`insert` rather than `modify`. The former is compatible with the std container apis and has familiar (and much simpler) semantics wrt re-insertion failure.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "author_replies": [
        "c:5006586379",
        "c:5027545920"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": true,
      "settled_by_id": "c:5027545920",
      "settled_by_quote": "I've changed all of the `modify` to `extract` then `insert`"
    }
  ],
  "support": [
    {
      "id": "c:4974409897",
      "verdict": "Concept ACK",
      "reason": "multi_index seems like the right thing to use here. Since this doesn't leak into consensus/node, I don't see the harm in spreading the dependency to wallet.",
      "substantive": true
    },
    {
      "id": "r:4892836862",
      "verdict": "Concept ACK",
      "reason": "Replace two containers — mapWallet and wtxOrdered — with a single boost::multi_index_container that owns the CWalletTx objects and provides both lookups natively. Most importantly, eliminates the raw pointer indirection and the synchronisation burden of keeping two containers in sync.",
      "substantive": true
    },
    {
      "id": "r:5026667636",
      "verdict": "ACK",
      "reason": "incidentally fixes a real bug on master: ReorderTransactions() mutates each CWalletTx::nOrderPos in place but never touches wtxOrdered... This PR's multi_index refactor makes that bug structurally impossible, since nOrderPos is the sort key of the ordered index itself — any mutation has to go through extract()+insert(), which re-sorts automatically.",
      "substantive": true
    },
    {
      "id": "c:5427418382",
      "verdict": "Concept ACK",
      "reason": "This also scratches the itch of renaming/removing the variable name mapWallet - it was not an intuitive name and didn't represent what the object contained within it.",
      "substantive": true
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Initial assessment of the PR. theuni's requests to use explicit index tags and extract/insert semantics instead of modify are recorded as non-blocking claims and were resolved in a subsequent push."
}
